{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1095173-mythos-based-faction","id":1095173,"title":"Mythos Based Faction?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-05-21T10:56:34-07:00","id":1095173,"title":"Mythos Based Faction?","content":"I've just finished reading Winter Tide by Ruthanna Emrys which has some excellent low key Life magic in it and I was wondering if there is a write up anywhere of a Mage faction that uses a Cthulhu mythos paradigm? i.e. One whose magic is based on principles such as the 'complete irrelevance of mankind in the face of the cosmic horrors that apparently exist in the universe', the worship of powerful but uncaring gods, and that uses symbology, mathematics, and lots of books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11490-dogstar","name":"Dogstar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11490_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-21T11:06:26-07:00","id":1095177,"title":"","content":"One of the Nephandi factions basically worship the Great Old Ones, or at least their equivalent in the WoD.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-21T11:06:44-07:00","id":1095178,"title":"","content":"That's basically the Nephandi.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-21T11:46:37-07:00","id":1095189,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1095173-mythos-based-faction?p=1095178#post1095178\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's basically the Nephandi.</div> </div> </div> </div>While some sources make it sound like it's the case for all Nephandi, others - like 2nd <i>the Book of Madness </i>say it's the K'llashaa who do so.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dogstar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1095173-mythos-based-faction#post1095173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> One whose magic is based on principles such as the 'complete irrelevance of mankind in the face of the cosmic horrors that apparently exist in the universe', the worship of powerful but uncaring gods, and that uses symbology, mathematics, and lots of books.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can use the K'llashaa. But I'd say any Mage could very well use the practices and Foci that you mentioned - without necessarily being part of the Nephandi.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-21T12:28:30-07:00","id":1095206,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1095173-mythos-based-faction?p=1095189#post1095189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While some sources make it sound like it's the case for all Nephandi, others - like 2nd <i>the Book of Madness </i>say it's the K'llashaa who do so.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was thinking more of the paradigm in a broader sense. The basic underlying cosmic horror idea is pretty fundamental to all the Nephandi, summoning tentacle monsters from beyond time and space is more a way of expressing that underlying idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-21T15:19:17-07:00","id":1095259,"title":"","content":"While the K'llashaa Nephandi are all about summoning the great old ones...the less unsavory magic users of Lovecraft, like Henry Armitage (who uses magic powders against the Dunwich Horror, if I remember correctly), can be represented very well by Hermetics and other mystics (especially those with experience in fighting K'llashaa).<br /> <br /> While Mage tend to be very humanistic, that doesn't mean <i>all mages</i> are humanistic. Mad Scientists may believe the world was created by terrible aliens, Hermetics know about horrible spirits from the outer darkness, Verbena summon old Chthonic deities that may have had older forms than those given in common mythology. Even in such a humanistic place like the Technocracy you can find Void Engineer veterans that have been too close to the horrors from beyond to be optimistic about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-21T16:19:31-07:00","id":1095275,"title":"","content":"Also the odd Marauder or three.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-21T16:48:14-07:00","id":1095287,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1095173-mythos-based-faction?p=1095259#post1095259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While the K'llashaa Nephandi are all about summoning the great old ones...the less unsavory magic users of Lovecraft, like Henry Armitage (who uses magic powders against the Dunwich Horror, if I remember correctly), can be represented very well by Hermetics and other mystics (especially those with experience in fighting K'llashaa).<br /> <br /> While Mage tend to be very humanistic, that doesn't mean <i>all mages</i> are humanistic. Mad Scientists may believe the world was created by terrible aliens, Hermetics know about horrible spirits from the outer darkness, Verbena summon old Chthonic deities that may have had older forms than those given in common mythology. Even in such a humanistic place like the Technocracy you can find Void Engineer veterans that have been too close to the horrors from beyond to be optimistic about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hell. Look at Iteration X. They believe the world functions on rules and in hard fate. You WILL do what you were destined to do because there is nothing else that could possibly happen. That's hardly humanistic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-21T17:24:36-07:00","id":1095300,"title":"","content":"Yes, while god-machine doesn't appear in the Mythos, there's a lot of potential for &quot;cosmic horror&quot; in that imaginary.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also the odd Marauder or three.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed. A few things I want to note:<br /> One of the known ways for mages to become Marauder (the others being a bad Awakening, and lots of Paradox) it's to do extended travels to the Deep Umbra. The most powerful Marauders come from there (like Medea, but really, if you've got what it takes to survive there enough time to go insane, and then come back, you're strong)<br /> <br /> Also, the most insane Marauders in exitsence, those whose Silence reached the 10 point roam the Deep Umbra, because they're too toxic for the Tellurian to tolerate<br /> <br /> Finally, there's an insanity inducing creature in Infinite Tapestry,<b> Lakleeb, The Lightless</b>. It's said that that Lakleeb it's, perhaps, older than the Tellurian itself. More a sentient force than a Umbrood, it has unfathomable power, can appear inside Earth seemingly without difficulty, and every time it does disaster happens. No one has spoken with it and remained sane, thus it's said that it's secrets are locked in the minds of lunatics...or Marauders","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 05-21-2017, 08:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-22T07:28:21-07:00","id":1095469,"title":"","content":"One less-used idea angle for Lovecraftian mage is Taft\u00e2ni. It is mostly based on Abd-al-Hazred the Mad, author of Kitab al-Azif, later translated as Necronomicon. Alhazred was a poet, and poetry is a important form of magic among Taft\u00e2ni (especially Kahin). Al-Azif means nocturnal whistling of wind in desert, thought to be voice of djinns, and of course, Taft\u00e2ni are most important masters of these. One must wonder why al-Hazred is known as a madman, while Taft\u00e2ni strive for clarity and truth; there can be two answers to this - al-Azif might be failed in his quest for truth; but more probably, he was successful, but the truth he obtained was too far beyond mundane. Irem of Many Pillars also has a place in both Mythos and Taft\u00e2ni myths.<br /> <br /> Using fanon of Djinn as fae creatures, it is possible also to link Taft\u00e2ni with Dreaming and then, with Lovecraft's Dreamland. However, there is a group more directly inspired by it in the World of Darkness - sorcerers of Zolondrodere, or Silver Portal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6231-mindszenty","name":"mindszenty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-22T08:34:35-07:00","id":1095487,"title":"","content":"Another lovecraftian font of Mage it's represented by those mages with the Demesne Background, Lucid Dreaming, or other dream-walkers. A Mage with Demesne can be the lord of his own persistent realm in the dream zone, which has a lot of reminiscences to certain Dreamer characters of the lovecraftian mythos (in particular the one that it's a beggar in the real life, but a powerful king in the Dream it's totally doable).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-23T02:57:58-07:00","id":1095813,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dogstar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1095173-mythos-based-faction#post1095173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> One whose magic is based on principles such as the 'complete irrelevance of mankind in the face of the cosmic horrors that apparently exist in the universe', the worship of powerful but uncaring gods, and that uses symbology, mathematics, and lots of books.</div> </div> </div> </div>Another aspect of the Mythos that could be visible in a Mage's Foci is faith and religion. The K'llashaa are noted as not following the standard hierarchy/titles of the Nephandi (Shaytan, Prelati...), but instead forming their own hierarchies with the leader being a priest. The K'llashaa are noted as using minimal(istic) foci, so I could see their True Magick being somehow similar to that of Choristers perhaps.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 05-24-2017, 05:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-28T02:23:26-07:00","id":1097718,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dogstar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1095173-mythos-based-faction#post1095173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've just finished reading Winter Tide by Ruthanna Emrys which has some excellent low key Life magic in it and I was wondering if there is a write up anywhere of a Mage faction that uses a Cthulhu mythos paradigm? i.e. One whose magic is based on principles such as the 'complete irrelevance of mankind in the face of the cosmic horrors that apparently exist in the universe', the worship of powerful but uncaring gods, and that uses symbology, mathematics, and lots of books.</div> </div> </div> </div>Since most of the Traditions are umbrella factions, you can easily justify a Dreamspeaker or a Verbena or even a Hermetic with this paradigm. Sons of Ether would work too. In fact Akashics and VAs are the only ones I can't immediately shoehorn into such mindset.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-28T15:03:40-07:00","id":1097879,"title":"","content":"I don't see how you can get a Hermetic or one of the Sons of Ether under that sort of umbrella. The Sons are all about 'Anything is Possible with Science.' since humans have science, it therefor follows that humans are not irrelevant. As for the Hermetics, while you get more variance under their umbrella than the Sons. (An odd thing to say given the weirdness of the Sons.) Some of their core features are essentially &quot;We are Gods chosen children. We ultimately wield more power than even the angels. We just have to learn how to use it.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-28T15:22:29-07:00","id":1097887,"title":"","content":"I could see some really fringe sons of ether trying to reverse engineer some mi-go technology.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","name":"BurritoMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13009_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"585"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-28T17:19:38-07:00","id":1097909,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't see how you can get a Hermetic or one of the Sons of Ether under that sort of umbrella. The Sons are all about 'Anything is Possible with Science.' since humans have science, it therefor follows that humans are not irrelevant. As for the Hermetics, while you get more variance under their umbrella than the Sons. (An odd thing to say given the weirdness of the Sons.) Some of their core features are essentially &quot;We are Gods chosen children. We ultimately wield more power than even the angels. We just have to learn how to use it.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Those are party lines, but mages tend to have beliefs of their own. Hermetics tend to follow their party line, but some weirdos on Ex-Miscelanea may diverge (as they always do).<br /> <br /> Etherites on the other hand...<br /> <br /> 1\u00b0 &quot;Anything is Possible with Science&quot; in no way implies that everything it's possible with <i>human science</i>. On the contrary, a faction among the Etherites believe that the best Science! it's that of aliens, the Ufologists are all about recovering pieces of alien technology, they're all about alien conspiration theories saying that all science comes from outer space. And then there's the ones that believe that the best Science comes from Atlantis and other lost civilizations (which don't need to be all utopical, after all, where's the adventure in that!).<br /> <br /> 2\u00b0 The Wall of Troy analogy that defines Etherite Paradigm openly refuses the idea that science knows everything, on the contrary, it points out that the human experience it's very limmited. The unknown, the rejected, all that lies outside the wall (outside human understanding of the cosmos) utterly dwarves everything that science has produced up to now. And the unknown cannot be just ignored to preserve our safe little world. The unknown, the outside, it's dangerous precisely because we don't know it, and thus we aren't prepared to face it, thus Troy it's destined to fall...unless we go outside and bring the unknown inside on our therms.<br /> Etherites aren't about the intrinsic value of humanity, they are about admiting that humans don know everything, that human knowledge isn't perfect...and then going foward and explore, to increase the amount of stuff that humanity knows. That's Science! <hr />I can see a Lovecraftian Etherite: A Mad Scientist, Ufologist, and a scientist-mystic, that study the ancient &quot;magic&quot; of the old ones (trully, it's not magic, it's jsut technology so advanced that it's indistinguishable from magic to normal humans that haven't enough vision). Madness and horror could be the result of his careless experiments, or the consequenmce of opening one tumb to many...but really, the potential it's there, you just need to let it be.<br /> <br /> All scientists believe I'm mad, I will show them who's mad!...every Etherite from Frankenstain to <a href=\"https://es.wikipedia.org/wiki/Herbert_West:_reanimador\" target=\"_blank\">Herbert West</a> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 05-28-2017, 08:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-28T20:40:46-07:00","id":1097958,"title":"","content":"I distinctly remember a Lovecraft story about a scientist inventing a machine, which stimulated a part of the brain or something. This making it possible to expand the senses of those around the machine while activated, allowing them to see creatures in another dimension while in total darkness. Basically, a Spirit 1 effect. The...things on the other side were, naturally, disturbing. Worse, the machine attracted their attention.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-28T23:53:10-07:00","id":1098005,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1095173-mythos-based-faction?p=1097879#post1097879\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't see how you can get a Hermetic or one of the Sons of Ether under that sort of umbrella. The Sons are all about 'Anything is Possible with Science.' since humans have science, it therefor follows that humans are not irrelevant. As for the Hermetics, while you get more variance under their umbrella than the Sons. (An odd thing to say given the weirdness of the Sons.) Some of their core features are essentially &quot;We are Gods chosen children. We ultimately wield more power than even the angels. We just have to learn how to use it.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Sons of Ether. Lovecraft's novels increasingly went towards sci-fi as he wrote. Mi-Go are space aliens, Elder Gods are bigger space aliens, magic is super-science. &quot;I made pact with Nyarlathotep and can use 4-th dimensional math to bend space-time&quot; is a perfectly functional Etherite concept.<br /> <br /> Hermetics would be essentially the same, but with more focus on the pact and less focus on the math. The M20 description of hermetics mentions exactly none of the things you are talking about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-29T06:39:45-07:00","id":1098091,"title":"","content":"Yeah, hermetics would treat the entities as ancient and mad deities, instead of aliens. Sure, they, being humans, can have power over them...so can Lovecraft humans have power over the supernatural with knowledge of the Elder Sign or other magics.<br /> <br /> Armitage was able to end the rampage of the son of an Elder God with a few friends, shotguns, and magic powders. As the librarian of Miskatonic and as one seemingly sane person that read the Necronomicon, he's a perfect Lovecraftian Mage and I don't see why he couldn't be a Hermetic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 05-29-2017, 09:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-29T10:43:46-07:00","id":1098147,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1095173-mythos-based-faction?p=1097958#post1097958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I distinctly remember a Lovecraft story about a scientist inventing a machine, which stimulated a part of the brain or something. This making it possible to expand the senses of those around the machine while activated, allowing them to see creatures in another dimension while in total darkness. Basically, a Spirit 1 effect. The...things on the other side were, naturally, disturbing. Worse, the machine attracted their attention.</div> </div> </div> </div>Tillinghast.<br /> <br /> Though Tillinghast's machine did pretty much the same thing as the Powder of Ibn Ghazi with the same consequences. So, tomayto, tomahto. Two different Foci producing the same effect in different ways.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-07T00:39:10-07:00","id":1101137,"title":"","content":"In my opinion what you ask is a 'World of Gods and Monsters' as defined in M20. Many mages can have it and it doesn't require Lovecraft in any sense or part to function.For a verbana it is a world of gods and monsters for whom man is nothing but toys and chattel. For a hermetic it is an universe filled with ancient daemons and beings who only understand the WILL and the POWER.<br /> Progenitor sees and world of Life at it's primal where man are but a particularly clever animal, still following it's instincts to a fault, and where murder/rape/cannibalism is a perfectly valid, natural and understandable things.<br /> Remove the purple prose from Lovecraft and it has nothing distinguishing left, just one more monster in the World of Darkness. .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4340-warpwind","name":"Warpwind","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4340_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}